---
import './design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from './SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from './SketchArrow.astro';
---
<figure id="product-attributes-map" class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface attributes-map wide" aria-labelledby="attributes-map-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Row boundaries</span>
  <h3 id="attributes-map-title">Three arrangements for the same capacity</h3>
  <p>Each arrangement records that P7, the Blue mug, holds 350 ml. The outline marks a stored row. A JSON field stays inside its product row; a related details record has its own row.</p>
  <div class="attribute-arrangements">
    <div class="arrangement">
      <h4>Typed product column</h4>
      <SketchSheet class="main-row">
        <p class="boundary-label">products · one row</p>
        <dl><div><dt>product_id</dt><dd>P7</dd></div><div><dt>name</dt><dd>Blue mug</dd></div><div><dt>current_price</dt><dd>EUR 20</dd></div></dl>
        <div class="capacity-field"><div><span>capacity_ml</span><strong>350</strong></div><small>integer column</small></div>
      </SketchSheet>
      <p class="arrangement-rule">A column type applies directly to the capacity. A separate CHECK can require it to be positive.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="arrangement">
      <h4>Embedded JSON</h4>
      <SketchSheet class="main-row">
        <p class="boundary-label">products · one row</p>
        <dl><div><dt>product_id</dt><dd>P7</dd></div><div><dt>name</dt><dd>Blue mug</dd></div><div><dt>current_price</dt><dd>EUR 20</dd></div></dl>
        <div class="json-field"><span>attributes · JSON column</span><div><span aria-hidden="true">{'{'}</span><div class="json-entry"><code>"capacity_ml":</code><strong>350</strong></div><span aria-hidden="true">{'}'}</span></div><small>Key and value inside an object</small></div>
      </SketchSheet>
      <p class="arrangement-rule">The column accepts valid JSON. An object check controls the outer shape; a capacity rule needs its own expression.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="arrangement">
      <h4>Related details row</h4>
      <SketchSheet>
        <p class="boundary-label">products · one row</p>
        <dl><div class="identity-field"><dt>product_id</dt><dd>P7</dd></div><div><dt>name</dt><dd>Blue mug</dd></div><div><dt>current_price</dt><dd>EUR 20</dd></div></dl>
      </SketchSheet>
      <div class="detail-reference"><span class="reference-arrow"><SketchArrow direction="down" /></span><p><code>product_id</code> foreign key<br />names the product above</p></div>
      <SketchSheet class="details-row" tone="teal">
        <p class="boundary-label">mug_details · another row</p>
        <dl><div class="identity-field"><dt>product_id</dt><dd>P7</dd></div><div class="capacity-field"><dt>capacity_ml</dt><dd>350</dd></div></dl>
        <small>product_id is also the primary key: at most one details row per product.</small>
      </SketchSheet>
      <p class="arrangement-rule">Capacity has a typed column in the details row. Requiring a details row for every mug is a further rule.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>The capacity is a product fact in all three arrangements. A related row separates where it is stored; an object nests it inside a value. Neither move, by itself, removes a duplicated fact. Other attributes are omitted, and the outlines show row boundaries rather than storage sizes.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .attributes-map.wide { margin-left:50%; }
  .attribute-arrangements { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1.3rem; margin-top:1.5rem; }
  .arrangement { min-width:0; }
  .arrangement h4 { min-height:2.6rem; }
  .arrangement :global(.main-row) { min-height:19rem; }
  .boundary-label { font:.7rem var(--font-mono); color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin:0 0 .7rem !important; }
  dl { margin:0; }
  dl > div { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto; gap:.4rem; padding:.4rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); font-size:.8125rem; }
  dt { overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  dd { margin:0; text-align:right; }
  .capacity-field { padding:.5rem; background:var(--paper-match); border-left:1px solid var(--teal); margin-top:.6rem; }
  .capacity-field > div { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:.5rem; }
  .capacity-field strong { font-weight:500; }
  .capacity-field small { display:block; color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin-top:.3rem; font-size:.7rem; }
  .json-field { border-left:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); margin-top:.6rem; padding:.5rem; background:var(--paper-match); }
  .json-field > span { font-size:.75rem; }
  .json-field > div { display:flex; gap:.3rem; align-items:center; font:1.9rem/2 var(--font-mono); margin:.2rem 0; }
  .json-entry { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:baseline; gap:.3rem; font:.75rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  .json-entry strong { font-weight:500; }
  .json-field small,.arrangement :global(.details-row) small { display:block; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.7rem; line-height:1.5; }
  .detail-reference { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.6rem; height:4.5rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .reference-arrow { display:block; transform:rotate(180deg); }
  .reference-arrow :global(.sketch-arrow) { width:2rem; height:3.5rem; }
  .detail-reference p { font-size:.75rem; line-height:1.4; }
  .arrangement :global(.details-row) .capacity-field { margin-top:0; }
  .arrangement :global(.details-row) small { margin-top:.5rem; }
  .identity-field { border-left:1px solid var(--teal); padding-left:.5rem; background:var(--paper-match); }
  .arrangement-rule { font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.55; padding-top:.5rem; }
  @media(max-width:760px) { .attribute-arrangements { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:1.5rem; max-width:26rem; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto; } .arrangement h4 { min-height:0; } .arrangement :global(.main-row) { min-height:0; } }
</style>
